    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nCurrenlty a home with part commercial use, this is a versatile property with excellent potential in a highly sought-after location. \n\nSituated on Rochestown Avenue, this substantial property presents an exciting opportunity for buyers seeking a well-located home with excellent potential for reconfiguration and further enhancement. Permission has been granted for change of use from a part commercial/medical use to full residential use with minor internal alterations. Planning reference D26A/0594/WEB. Alternatively, the existing configuration lends itself particularly well to professional or business use, subject to the relevant permissions. Its prominent location, generous parking and proximity to local amenities make it an attractive proposition for a range of occupiers.\n\nThe property has historically operated as a combination of residential accommodation and a dental surgery and, while currently arranged for this purpose, it benefits from a layout that can be readily adapted back to a comfortable family home. Planning permission is also underway to facilitate the change of use back to full residential use, offering buyers a clear pathway to realise the property's full potential.\n\nOn entering, the existing entrance hall currently serves as the reception area for the dental practice. To the front, the original reception room has been adapted as a waiting room, while the former garage, together with the rear extension, provides a series of treatment rooms. Importantly, the original staircase remains intact, making the reinstatement of the property's residential layout particularly straightforward.\n\nTo the rear, the property opens into a generous open-plan kitchen, living and dining area, creating a bright and sociable space with direct connection to the rear garden. A spiral staircase provides access to the first-floor level, where there are currently three bedrooms and a family bathroom, together with the additional room that provides the access to the spiral staircase, which would have originally served as a fourth generous bedroom. \n \nThe location is superb. Rochestown Avenue is an established and highly convenient address in Glenageary, with an excellent selection of local amenities close at hand. The area is particularly well served by a range of renowned primary and secondary schools, while shopping, cafés, restaurants and everyday conveniences are all readily accessible.\nFor commuters, the property enjoys easy access to the M50 and Dublin's wider road network, while the surrounding area is well served by public transport options, providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding suburbs."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance hall: - 2.73m x 3.04m\npart wood panelled walls, hall to set into extensive glazing allowing the light to fill the area, storage closet. Open through to what is currently a reception.\n\nReception area: - 2.29m x 2.90m\nlaminate floor, fitted wall on floor units\n\nGuest WC: - \ntiled floor, sink with under sink storage, tiled splash back, w.c.\n\nLobby: - 5.45m x 2.44m\nlaminate floor, fitted storage, breakfast counter, pedestrian side access\n\nSurgery 1: - 3.56m x 2.44m\nlinoleum floor, fitted storage, two sinks, large window allowing excellent natural light, overlooking the front\n\nBathroom: - \nlaminate floor, sink, w.c..\n\nSurgery 2: - 3.87m x 2.90m\nlaminate floor, fitted wall and floor storage, three sinks, light filled\n\nReception Room/Waiting Room: - 4.87m x 3.20m\nnicely appointed, fitted shelving, access through to the residential part of the property\n\nResidential Duplex Property - \n\n\nGround Floor - \n\n\nLiving/Dining: - 10.00m x 4.52m\ndouble doors from the garden, light well, recessed lighting, wood floors\n\nKitchen: - 5.31m x 1.88m max\nlinoleum floor, fitted shaker style units, wall mounted shelving, washing machine, feature wood panelled wall, an archway connect the kitchen with the living dining area and also creates a breakfast counter, pedestrian side access\n\nFirst floor - \n\n\nBedroom 1: - 4.87m x 3.20m\nwall to wall light bearing window, extensive built-in storage and wardrobes\n\nBedroom 2: - 4.04m x 3.94m\nwall to wall windows, built-in wardrobe\n\nBathroom: - 2.27m x 1.99m\nbath with shower, part tiled walls, w.c., w.h.b.\n\nBedroom 3: - 2.30m x 3.94m\nbuilt in storage incorporating a desk\n\nLanding / Bedroom 4: - 3.85m x 3.20m\nonce the fourth bedroom, this is now a very large landing giving access to the spiral staircase to the ground floor or level\n\nGarden - \nOutside, the property enjoys a lovely, private rear garden. There is a decked area with steps down to a garden laid mainly in lawn bordered with mature hedging. To the front of the house there is off street parking and a low maintenance pebbled garden with mature hedging.\n\n"
      },
